@anon.db70647216840ea9fd0320153731fc7a.443 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [686 x i8] }> <{ [686 x i8] c"Exposes a value to the query system without producing visible content.\0A\0AThis element can be retrieved with the [`query`] function and from the\0Acommand line with [`typst query`]($reference/meta/query/#cli-queries). Its\0Apurpose is to expose an arbitrary value to the introspection system. To\0Aidentify a metadata value among others, you can attach a [`label`] to it and\0Aquery for that label.\0A\0AThe `metadata` element is especially useful for command line queries because\0Ait allows you to expose arbitrary values to the outside world.\0A\0A```example\0A// Put metadata somewhere.\0A#metadata(\22This is a note\22) <note>\0A\0A// And find it from anywhere else.\0A#context {\0A  query(<note>).first().value\0A}\0A```" }>, align 1
